# #127, ADR-0911: a command of a tier the core build leaves out is refused by name, with the
# stable code `resolve.not_in_build` and the status of a command that is found and cannot be
# executed (126) — never a parse error, never a panic, never a search of PATH that ends in
# "command not found". One command per tier, the flags of the remote tier, and a stage of a
# compiled-out tier in the middle of a pipeline.
case: a command of a compiled-out tier refuses by name, naming its tier
profile: core
run: |
  refuse() {
    ono -c "$1" 2>&1 | head -1
    ono -c "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo "status=$?"
  }
  refuse 'map'
  refuse 'find place nginx'
  refuse 'trace process 1'
  refuse 'get process | where pid == 1 | trace process'
  refuse 'load plugin dev.example.tool'
  refuse 'echo:emit'
  refuse 'link host example'
  refuse 'at -1h'
  refuse 'get process --at -1h'
  refuse 'plan remove file /tmp/nothing-here'
  refuse 'adapt ls'
  ono --agent 2>&1 | head -1
  ono --print-peer-key 2>&1 | head -1
  echo "== what ran instead: nothing =="
  ono -c 'exec:ls /usr/local/bin'
exit: 0
stdout-contains: `map` belongs to the spatial systems interface (spec v0.4), which this core build of ono does not include
stdout-contains: `trace process` belongs to the relationship graph and `trace` (spec §22)
stdout-contains: belongs to the KUANG/11 plugin runtime (spec §31)
stdout-contains: `link host` belongs to remote links and the agent (spec §21)
stdout-contains: belongs to the temporal and causal systems interface (spec v0.5)
stdout-contains: `--at` belongs to the temporal and causal systems interface
stdout-contains: belongs to prospective change, protection and recovery (spec v0.6)
stdout-contains: `adapt` belongs to the external command adapters (spec v0.3)
stdout-contains: `--agent` belongs to remote links and the agent
stdout-contains: `--print-peer-key` belongs to remote links and the agent
stdout-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0104 resolve.not_in_build
stdout-not-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0101
stdout-not-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0001
stdout-not-contains: panicked
stdout-not-contains: status=0
stdout-not-contains: status=127
stdout-matches: ^status=126$
stdout-matches: ^ono$
